---Class representing a Traffic Manager endpoint properties.
---@class azure.trafficmanager.EndpointProperties
---@field targetResourceId? string The Azure Resource URI of the of the endpoint. Not applicable to endpoints of type 'ExternalEndpoints'.
---@field target? string The fully-qualified DNS name or IP address of the endpoint. Traffic Manager returns this value in DNS responses to direct traffic to this endpoint.
---@field endpointStatus? azure.trafficmanager.EndpointStatus|string The status of the endpoint. If the endpoint is Enabled, it is probed for endpoint health and is included in the traffic routing method.
---@field weight? number The weight of this endpoint when using the 'Weighted' traffic routing method. Possible values are from 1 to 1000.
---@field priority? number The priority of this endpoint when using the 'Priority' traffic routing method. Possible values are from 1 to 1000, lower values represent higher priority. This is an optional parameter. If specified, it must be specified on all endpoints, and no two endpoints can share the same priority value.
---@field endpointLocation? string Specifies the location of the external or nested endpoints when using the 'Performance' traffic routing method.
---@field endpointMonitorStatus? azure.trafficmanager.EndpointMonitorStatus|string The monitoring status of the endpoint.
---@field minChildEndpoints? number The minimum number of endpoints that must be available in the child profile in order for the parent profile to be considered available. Only applicable to endpoint of type 'NestedEndpoints'.
---@field minChildEndpointsIPv4? number The minimum number of IPv4 (DNS record type A) endpoints that must be available in the child profile in order for the parent profile to be considered available. Only applicable to endpoint of type 'NestedEndpoints'.
---@field minChildEndpointsIPv6? number The minimum number of IPv6 (DNS record type AAAA) endpoints that must be available in the child profile in order for the parent profile to be considered available. Only applicable to endpoint of type 'NestedEndpoints'.
---@field geoMapping? azure.trafficmanager.EndpointPropertiesGeoMappingList The list of countries/regions mapped to this endpoint when using the 'Geographic' traffic routing method. Please consult Traffic Manager Geographic documentation for a full list of accepted values.
---@field subnets? azure.trafficmanager.EndpointPropertiesSubnetsList The list of subnets, IP addresses, and/or address ranges mapped to this endpoint when using the 'Subnet' traffic routing method. An empty list will match all ranges not covered by other endpoints.
---@field customHeaders? azure.trafficmanager.EndpointPropertiesCustomHeadersList List of custom headers.
---@field alwaysServe? azure.trafficmanager.AlwaysServe|string If Always Serve is enabled, probing for endpoint health will be disabled and endpoints will be included in the traffic routing method.

